1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:01,800
Matthew 6.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:09,360
Beware of practicing your righteousness before other people, in order to be seen by them.

3
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:13,020
For then you will have no reward from your Father who is in heaven.

4
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:19,500
Thus, when you give to the needy, sound no trumpet before you as the hypocrites do in

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:23,380
the synagogues and in the streets, that they may be praised by others.

6
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:26,940
Truly I say to you, they have received their reward.

7
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:31,920
But when you give to the needy, do not let your left hand know what your right hand is

8
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:37,980
doing, so that your giving may be in secret, and your Father who sees in secret will reward

9
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:38,300
you.

10
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:45,540
And when you pray, you must not be like the hypocrites, for they love to stand and pray

11
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:49,900
in the synagogues and at the street corners, that they may be seen by others.

12
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:54,000
Truly I say to you, they have received their reward.

13
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,920
But when you pray, go into your room.

14
00:00:56,940 --> 00:01:03,080
And shut the door, and pray to your Father who is in secret, and your Father who sees

15
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:04,900
in secret will reward you.

16
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:11,980
And when you pray, do not heap up empty phrases as the Gentiles do, for they think that they

17
00:01:11,980 --> 00:01:13,800
will be heard for their many words.

18
00:01:14,480 --> 00:01:19,200
Do not be like them, for your Father knows what you need, before you ask Him.

19
00:01:20,060 --> 00:01:25,440
Pray then like this, Our Father in heaven, hallowed be your name.

20
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:26,920
Your kingdom come.

21
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:29,760
Your will be done on earth as it is in heaven.

22
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:37,160
Give us this day our daily bread, and forgive us our debts, as we also have forgiven our

23
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:37,640
debtors.

24
00:01:38,180 --> 00:01:42,280
And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil.

25
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:48,640
For if you forgive others their trespasses, your heavenly Father will also forgive you.

26
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:55,640
But if you do not forgive others their trespasses, neither will your Father forgive your trespasses.

27
00:01:56,940 --> 00:02:03,460
And when you fast, do not look gloomy like the hypocrites, for they disfigure their faces

28
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:05,860
that their fasting may be seen by others.

29
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:09,640
Truly I say to you, they have received their reward.

30
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:16,040
But when you fast, anoint your head and wash your face, that your fasting may not be seen

31
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:22,160
by others, but by your Father who is in secret, and your Father who sees in secret will reward

32
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:22,480
you.

33
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:26,700
Do not lay up for yourselves treasures on earth.

34
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,460
Where moth and rust destroy and where thieves break in and steal.

35
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:37,120
But lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust destroys, and where

36
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:38,760
thieves do not break in and steal.

37
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:43,200
For where your treasure is, there your heart will be also.

38
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:46,900
The eye is the lamp of the body.

39
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:51,060
So if your eye is healthy, your whole body will be full of light.

40
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:55,200
But if your eye is bad, your whole body will be full of darkness.

41
00:02:55,860 --> 00:02:55,960
Glory in the name of Jesus.

42
00:02:55,980 --> 00:02:56,300
Glory in the name of Jesus.

43
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:56,900
Glory in the name of Jesus.

44
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:56,920
Glory in the name of Jesus.

45
00:02:56,920 --> 00:02:56,940
Glory in the name of Jesus.

46
00:02:56,940 --> 00:03:04,240
in you is darkness. How great is the darkness! No one can serve two masters, for either he will

47
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:09,180
hate the one and love the other, or he will be devoted to the one and despise the other.

48
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:17,340
You cannot serve God and money. Therefore I tell you, do not be anxious about your life,

49
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:22,360
what you will eat or what you will drink, nor about your body, what you will put on.

50
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:28,620
Is not life more than food, and the body more than clothing? Look at the birds of the air.

51
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:34,860
They neither sow nor reap, nor gather into barns, and yet your heavenly Father feeds them.

52
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:40,240
Are you not of more value than they? And which of you, by being anxious,

53
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:46,780
can add a single hour to his span of life? And why are you anxious about clothing?

54
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:52,340
Consider the lilies of the field, how they grow. They neither toil nor spin.

55
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:58,020
Yet I tell you, even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of these.

56
00:03:58,580 --> 00:04:04,000
But if God so clothes the grass of the field, which today is alive and tomorrow is thrown

57
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:12,240
into the oven, will he not much more clothe you? O you of little faith! Therefore do not be anxious,

58
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:17,040
saying, What shall we eat, or what shall we drink, or what shall we wear?

59
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:22,280
For the Gentiles seek after all these things, and your heavenly Father,

60
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:27,580
knows that you need them all. But seek first the kingdom of God and his righteousness,

61
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:33,300
and all these things will be added to you. Therefore do not be anxious about tomorrow,

62
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:39,300
for tomorrow will be anxious for itself. Sufficient for the day is its own trouble.

